      "filename": "Acorn Street Boston, Massachusetts.jpg",
      "title": "File:Acorn Street Boston, Massachusetts.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Acorn_Street_Boston%2C_Massachusetts.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acorn_Street_Boston,_Massachusetts.jpg",
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 1200,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Shawn M. Kent",
      "description": "Acorn Street is a historic and picturesque cobblestone street located in the renowned Beacon Hill neighborhood of Boston, Massachusetts, USA. This charming street has become a beloved attraction, drawing visitors from near and far. Acorn Street is characterized by its well-preserved row houses, constructed in brick and stone, which exude a timeless elegance. The street's gas lamps, quaint flower boxes, and narrow layout create a nostalgic ambiance, evoking the charm of the 19th century. Particularly during the autumn season, Acorn Street's beauty reaches new heights, as the vibrant foliage of the trees that line the street transforms into a stunning tapestry of red and orange hues. Although Acorn Street is a popular destination for tourists, its appeal extends beyond its visual splendor. The street provides a glimpse into Boston's rich history and serves as a living testament to the city's architectural heritage. Whether strolling along the cobblestones or admiring the captivating facades, a visit to Acorn Street offers a truly immersive experience in the heart of Boston's cultural tapestry.",
      "dateCreated": "2023-04-03 14:06:47",
      "sourceType": "poi",
      "sourceArticleId": "commonwealth-of-nations",
      "smallPath": "_m/tpc/co/mm/on/we/commonwealth-of-nations/acorn-street-boston-massachuse-small.webp"
